1
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:29,130
See you tomorrow.

2
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,484
Oh, my God!

3
00:02:12,131 --> 00:02:13,633
I'm in.

4
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,539
We're almost there.

5
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:12,669
- Sir, are you sure about this?
- I told you, we're going to be all right.

6
00:04:12,835 --> 00:04:18,299
I understand, sir. It's just that I'm scoping
some serious sentinel activity up here.

7
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:06,931
Still can't sleep?

8
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,268
You wanna talk?

9
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,981
They're just dreams.

10
00:05:17,316 --> 00:05:19,694
If you're afraid of something...

11
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:21,696
I just wish...

12
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:24,615
I wish I knew what I'm supposed to do.

13
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:26,617
That's all.

14
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:29,120
I just wish I knew.

15
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:33,541
She's gonna call. Don't worry.

16
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,751
Here you are.

17
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:38,379
- Are we ready to go?
- We're already late.

18
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:43,176
These geotherms confirm
the last transmission of the <i>Osiris.</i>

19
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:45,595
The machines are digging.

20
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:49,557
They're boring from the surface
down to Zion.

21
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:52,310
- Mother--
- They'll avoid the perimeter defense.

22
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:53,978
How fast are they moving?

23
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:57,523
Control estimates their descent
at 100 meters an hour.

24
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:00,151
- How deep are they?
- Almost 2000 meters.

25
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:03,863
- What about the scans from the <i>Osiris?</i>
- They can't be accurate.

26
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,948
- They may be.
- It's not possible.

27
00:06:06,115 --> 00:06:08,576
That'd mean there are
a quarter-million sentinels.

28
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:10,244
- That's right.
- That can't be.

29
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:12,080
Why not?

30
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:16,000
A sentinel for every man,
woman and child in Zion.

31
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:20,922
That sounds exactly like
the thinking of a machine to me.

32
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:23,257
Morpheus, glad you could join us.

33
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:24,926
Niobe.

34
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:29,680
My apologies to all.
But as you are undoubtedly aware...

35
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:33,142
...it's become difficult to locate
a secure broadcast position.

36
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:36,562
- Squiddies got our best spots.
- Lines are crawling with them.

37
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:40,525
And if Niobe's right, in 72 hours
there's gonna be a quarter-million more.

38
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:41,818
What are we gonna do?

39
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:44,278
We're gonna do what
Commander Lock ordered.

40
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:47,198
We'll evacuate broadcast level
and return to Zion.

41
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:52,495
And does the commander have a plan
for stopping 250,000 sentinels?

42
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:55,331
A strategy is still being formulated.

43
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:57,166
I'm sure it is.

44
00:07:12,181 --> 00:07:14,183
What do you think
we should do, Morpheus?

45
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:16,519
- Proceed as ordered...
- What is it?

46
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:17,728
I don't know.

47
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:20,690
...however, I must
ask one of you for help.

48
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:26,571
Some of you believe as I believe, some
of you do not. Those of you that do...

49
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:29,282
...know we are nearing
the end of our struggle.

50
00:07:29,448 --> 00:07:33,703
The prophecy will be fulfilled soon.
But before it can be...

51
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:37,206
...the Oracle must be consulted.

52
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:47,383
If we return and recharge now...

53
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:51,304
...we can be back in 36 hours, well
before the machines reach this depth.

54
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:53,347
Do you understand what you're asking?

55
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:56,350
I am asking that one ship
remain here in our place...

56
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:59,228
...in case the Oracle
should attempt to contact us.

57
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:02,523
Bullshit. You're asking one of us
to disobey a direct order.

58
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:07,236
That's right, I am. But we well know
that the reason most of us are here...

59
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:10,031
...is because of our affinity
for disobedience.

60
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:12,116
What happens when you
get back to Zion...

61
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,702
...and the commander
throws you in the stockade?

62
00:08:14,869 --> 00:08:16,078
He won't.

63
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:20,416
Goddamn it, Morpheus,
you ain't never gonna change.

64
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,878
Shit, I'll do it just to see
what Deadbolt does to you.

65
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:25,588
You got 36 hours.

66
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:30,218
I'm looking for Neo.

67
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:33,763
- Never heard of him.
- I have something for him.

68
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,183
A gift.

69
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,269
You see, he set me free.

70
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,941
Fine, whatever. Now piss off.

71
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:46,526
Who was that?

72
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:48,527
How did you know someone was here?

73
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:50,154
He gave you this.

74
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,328
He said you set him free.

75
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,624
Is everything all right, sir?

76
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,627
The meeting is over.
Retreat to your exits.

77
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,004
- Agents are coming.
- Agents?

78
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:08,839
Go.

79
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:19,725
Hiya, fellas.

80
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:21,018
- It's him.
- The anomaly.

81
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,436
- Do we proceed?
- Yes.

82
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:25,106
- He is still--
- Only human.

83
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:33,531
Hm. Upgrades.

84
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:31,005
- That went as expected.
- Yes.

85
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,841
It's happening exactly as before.

86
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:36,677
Well, not exactly.

87
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:28,854
Where are you?

88
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:37,113
This is the <i>Nebuchadnezzar,</i>
requesting access through Gate Three.

89
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:45,621
<i>Nebuchadnezzar,</i> this is Zion Control.
Maintain present velocity and stand by.

90
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,289
<i>Roger that, Control.</i>

91
00:11:47,456 --> 00:11:50,960
This is Control requesting immediate
stand-down of arms at Gate Three.

92
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:54,964
We have the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i>
on approach. Let's open her up.

93
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:03,472
<i>You are cleared through
Gate Three to Bay Seven.</i>

94
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:05,349
Roger that, Control.

95
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:15,568
Door's open, bed's made.
Welcome home.

96
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:18,487
No place like it.

97
00:12:32,668 --> 00:12:36,380
Roger that, Control. Zion Control,
stand by for Gate Three lockdown.

98
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:28,307
<i>The</i> Nebuchadnezzar <i>is down.
Bay Seven.</i>

99
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:29,642
Understood.

100
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,903
Captain Mifune.

101
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:43,155
Captain Morpheus.

102
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:46,158
Are you here to escort me
to the stockade, captain?

103
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,993
- I'm just here to keep the peace.
-

104
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:50,621
- Link.
- Sir?

105
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:53,374
I want the ship ready to go
as soon as possible.

106
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,084
Understood, sir.

107
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:20,526
- Morpheus.
- Commander Lock.

108
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:25,281
I spoke to the other captains. I wanted to
offer you a chance to explain your actions.

109
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:28,325
I wasn't aware that my actions
required any explanation.

110
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:30,786
You were given an order
to return to Zion.

111
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:33,789
- I did.
- You asked for one ship to remain behind.

112
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:36,625
I would have stayed,
but I needed to recharge my ship.

113
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:39,503
So you admit to a direct contravention
of your duty.

114
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:43,090
We need a presence inside the Matrix
to await contact from the Oracle.

115
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:45,217
I don't want to hear that shit!

116
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:48,053
I don't care about oracles
or prophecies or messiahs!

117
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:51,640
I care about one thing: Stopping that
army from destroying this city.

118
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:54,643
To do that I need soldiers
to obey my orders.

119
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:59,398
With all due respect, commander,
there is only one way to save our city.

120
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,983
How?

121
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:03,944
- Neo.
- Goddamn it, Morpheus.

122
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:06,739
Not everyone believes what you believe.

123
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,991
My beliefs do not require them to.

124
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:21,086
There's a gathering tonight. Everyone's
talking. A lot of people are scared.

125
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:24,006
No one remembers the last time
so many ships were docked.

126
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:27,134
- Something big is happening, isn't it?
- Hey.

127
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:30,471
We're not allowed to say anything,
so stop asking.

128
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:38,896
Goddamn, it's good to be home.

129
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:00,042
- Councillor Hamann.
- Commander.

130
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:03,420
- Captain.
- Councillor.

131
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:06,965
Council's asked me to speak tonight
at the temple gathering.

132
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:11,220
The presence of the fleet and the
persistence of rumors must be addressed.

133
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:13,889
The people must be told
what is happening.

134
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,766
Of course, councillor.

135
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:21,730
But might I advise a level of discretion
concerning specific details.

136
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:24,900
- We do not wish to start a panic.
- Quite right.

137
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:28,153
A panic is not what anyone wants.

138
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,657
What about you, captain?
What would you advise?

139
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:38,831
The truth. No one will panic,
because there is nothing to fear.

140
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,125
That army won't reach
the gates of Zion.

141
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:45,504
- What makes you so sure?
- Consider what we have seen, councillor.

142
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,548
Consider that in the past six months...

143
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:49,758
...we have freed more minds
than in six years.

144
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:52,928
This attack is an act of desperation.

145
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:56,932
I believe very soon the prophecy
will be fulfilled and this war will end.

146
00:16:58,809 --> 00:17:00,936
I hope you're right, captain.

147
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,814
I do not believe it to be
a matter of hope, councillor.

148
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,567
It is simply a matter of time.

149
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:10,195
My stop.

150
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:11,780
See you soon.

151
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:13,407
Hopefully not too soon.

152
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:16,744
Let's go, kid.
These two got things to do.

153
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,921
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

154
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:30,507
I am if you're thinking
this elevator is too slow.

155
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:34,011
- How long do we charge the <i>Neb?</i>
- Twenty-four, maybe 30 hours.

156
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:38,390
Some people go their entire lives
without hearing news that good.

157
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:07,169
Neo, please, I have a son,
Jacob, aboard the <i>Gnosis.</i>

158
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:10,839
- Please, watch over him.
- I'll try.

159
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:13,091
I have a daughter on the <i>Icarus.</i>

160
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:15,177
No, wait.

161
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,846
It's all right. They need you.

162
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:20,265
- I need you.
- I know.

163
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:23,101
There's time.

164
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:38,826
- They started yet?
- Only Councillor Hamann's opening prayer.

165
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:42,079
Tonight, let us honor
these men and women.

166
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,873
These are our soldiers, our warriors.

167
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:49,294
These are our husbands and wives,
our brothers and sisters...

168
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:51,129
...our children.

169
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:54,842
Let us remember those
that have been lost...

170
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:58,220
...and let us give thanks
for those that have been found...

171
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:01,682
...and who stand here beside us.

172
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:05,561
Now I would like someone else
to close this prayer...

173
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:08,939
...someone who hasn't spoken here
in a long time...

174
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:14,486
...but who I believe has something to say
that we all need to hear.

175
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:17,072
I give you Morpheus.

176
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:40,762
Zion! Hear me!

177
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:44,892
It is true what many of you have heard.

178
00:19:45,058 --> 00:19:49,062
The machines have gathered
an army, and as I speak...

179
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:53,150
...that army is drawing nearer to our home.

180
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:59,281
Believe me when I say we have
a difficult time ahead of us.

181
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:06,121
But if we are to be prepared for it,
we must first shed our fear of it.

182
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:11,543
I stand here before you now
truthfully unafraid.

183
00:20:12,127 --> 00:20:13,879
Why?

184
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:17,132
Because I believe something you do not?

185
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,134
No!

186
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:24,389
I stand here without fear
because I remember.

187
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:28,477
I remember that I am here not because
of the path that lies before me...

188
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:31,980
...but because of the path
that lies behind me.

189
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:36,818
I remember that for 100 years
we have fought these machines.

190
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:41,740
I remember that for 100 years
they have sent their armies to destroy us.

191
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:47,079
And after a century of war,
I remember that which matters most:

192
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:51,875
We are still here!

193
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,676
Tonight...

194
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:04,221
...let us send a message to that army.

195
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:07,432
Tonight, let us shake this cave.

196
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:11,478
Tonight, let us tremble these halls...

197
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:14,773
...of earth, steel and stone.

198
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:20,195
Let us be heard from red core
to black sky.

199
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:24,908
Tonight, let us make them remember:

200
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:30,038
This is Zion and we are not afraid!

201
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:09,870
Excuse me.

202
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:25,218
- I missed you.
- I can tell.

203
00:22:25,677 --> 00:22:29,389
I was thinking, everyone is here.

204
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:32,225
Follow me.

205
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:56,805
Neo, what is it?

206
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:59,349
What's wrong?

207
00:26:00,934 --> 00:26:03,270
It's okay, you can tell me.

208
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:06,147
Trinity...

209
00:26:06,314 --> 00:26:09,109
Don't be afraid.

210
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:11,611
I can't lose you.

211
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,655
You're not gonna lose me.

212
00:26:17,784 --> 00:26:20,662
You feel this?

213
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:22,622
I'm never letting go.

214
00:26:59,826 --> 00:27:02,495
Good night, Zion.

215
00:27:02,662 --> 00:27:05,332
Sweet dreams.

216
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:17,177
- You all right?
- I'll make it.

217
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:19,971
Did you see that agent?
I've never seen anything like that.

218
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:22,223
It doesn't matter.
All that matters is this.

219
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:24,684
You first.

220
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:38,448
- Oh, God.
- "Smith" will suffice.

221
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:53,671
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

222
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:46,933
- Care for some company?
- Councillor Hamann.

223
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:50,645
I don't want to intrude
if you'd prefer to be alone.

224
00:28:51,104 --> 00:28:54,649
- No, I could probably use some company.
- Good.

225
00:28:55,108 --> 00:28:57,485
So could I.

226
00:29:00,613 --> 00:29:03,116
It's nice tonight.

227
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:06,035
Very calm.

228
00:29:06,202 --> 00:29:08,955
It feels like everyone is sleeping
very peacefully.

229
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,791
Not everyone.

230
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:16,796
I hate sleeping.
I never sleep more than a few hours.

231
00:29:16,963 --> 00:29:21,009
I figure I slept the first 11 years
of my life, now I'm making up for it.

232
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:26,181
- What about you?
- I just haven't been able to sleep much.

233
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:30,810
- It's a good sign.
- Of what?

234
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:34,147
That you are in fact still human.

235
00:29:37,734 --> 00:29:41,654
Have you ever been
to the engineering level?

236
00:29:41,821 --> 00:29:44,866
I love to walk there at night.
It's quite amazing.

237
00:29:45,033 --> 00:29:47,577
- Would you like to see it?
- Sure.

238
00:29:58,254 --> 00:30:02,717
Almost no one comes down here.
Unless, of course, there's a problem.

239
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:07,972
That's how it is with people. Nobody cares
how it works as long as it works.

240
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:10,433
I like it down here.

241
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:16,397
I like to be reminded this city survives
because of these machines.

242
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:21,694
These machines are keeping us alive
while other machines are coming to kill us.

243
00:30:22,111 --> 00:30:26,950
Interesting, isn't it?
The power to give life...

244
00:30:27,116 --> 00:30:30,328
- ...and the power to end it.
- We have the same power.

245
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:33,206
Yeah, I suppose we do, but...

246
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:36,834
...sometimes I think about those people
still plugged into the Matrix.

247
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:40,004
And when I look at these machines...

248
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:45,260
...I can't help thinking that, in a way,
we are plugged into them.

249
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:48,429
But we control these machines,
they don't control us.

250
00:30:48,847 --> 00:30:51,850
Of course not. How could they?

251
00:30:52,016 --> 00:30:54,561
The idea is pure nonsense...

252
00:30:55,061 --> 00:30:58,189
...but it does make one wonder just...

253
00:30:58,356 --> 00:30:59,941
...what is control?

254
00:31:00,191 --> 00:31:03,236
If we wanted, we could
shut these machines down.

255
00:31:03,611 --> 00:31:08,074
Of course. That's it. You hit it.
That's control, isn't it?

256
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:12,078
If we wanted,
we could smash them to bits.

257
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:16,457
Although if we did, we'd have to consider
what would happen to our lights...

258
00:31:16,624 --> 00:31:19,294
...our heat, our air.

259
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:24,424
So we need machines and they need us.
Is that your point, councillor?

260
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:27,218
No. No point.

261
00:31:27,927 --> 00:31:32,015
Old men like me don't bother
with making points. There's no point.

262
00:31:32,807 --> 00:31:36,603
Is that why there are no young men
on the Council?

263
00:31:36,769 --> 00:31:38,438
Good point.

264
00:31:39,147 --> 00:31:43,318
Why don't you tell me
what's on your mind, councillor.

265
00:31:43,484 --> 00:31:46,738
There is so much in this world...

266
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:49,824
...that I do not understand.

267
00:31:51,618 --> 00:31:56,372
See that machine? It has something to do
with recycling our water supply.

268
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:59,542
I have absolutely no idea how it works.

269
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:03,796
But I do understand the reason
for it to work.

270
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:09,802
I have absolutely no idea how you
are able to do some of the things you do.

271
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:14,140
But I believe there's a reason for that
as well.

272
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:20,146
I only hope we understand that reason
before it's too late.

273
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:28,321
- Ballard.
- Is he here?

274
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:33,326
Neo, it's from the Oracle.

275
00:32:36,287 --> 00:32:37,080
It's time to go.

276
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:49,550
- Neo!
- How the hell--?

277
00:32:49,967 --> 00:32:52,136
Bane.

278
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:53,638
Is something wrong?

279
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:55,515
No, I'm fine.

280
00:32:55,682 --> 00:32:58,476
I just wanted to catch you to say...

281
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,478
...good luck.

282
00:33:02,146 --> 00:33:03,856
Thanks.

283
00:33:04,023 --> 00:33:06,442
We'll see you.

284
00:33:08,027 --> 00:33:11,114
Neo! Just in time.

285
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,616
- You're gonna see the Oracle?
- There's no time.

286
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:15,410
I had to give something to Neo.

287
00:33:16,119 --> 00:33:18,830
A gift from one of the orphans.

288
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:22,417
He made me swear to get it to you
before you left.

289
00:33:23,292 --> 00:33:25,753
He said you'd understand.

290
00:33:28,423 --> 00:33:30,550
Thanks.

291
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:40,560
I was just told you cleared
the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i> for takeoff.

292
00:33:40,727 --> 00:33:42,687
That is correct.

293
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:44,814
Am I still in charge
of our defense system?

294
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:46,274
Of course.

295
00:33:46,983 --> 00:33:51,028
I believe I need every ship we have
if we're going to survive this attack.

296
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,781
I understand that, commander.

297
00:33:53,948 --> 00:33:56,534
Then why did you allow
the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i> to leave?

298
00:33:56,701 --> 00:34:01,581
Because I believe our survival depends
on more than how many ships we have.

299
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:06,377
Be careful.

300
00:34:35,406 --> 00:34:37,617
Hello.

301
00:34:47,919 --> 00:34:51,464
- You seek the Oracle.
- Who are you?

302
00:34:54,509 --> 00:34:59,013
I am Seraph. I can take you to her,
but first I must apologize.

303
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:00,973
Apologize for what?

304
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:03,434
For this.

305
00:36:00,741 --> 00:36:02,994
Good.

306
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:08,666
The Oracle has many enemies.
I had to be sure.

307
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,043
- Of what?
- That you are the One.

308
00:36:11,502 --> 00:36:15,256
- You could have just asked.
- No. You do not truly know someone...

309
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:17,675
...until you fight them.

310
00:36:18,217 --> 00:36:21,679
Come. She's waiting.

311
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:38,613
Where the hell did they go?

312
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:41,699
These are back doors, aren't they?

313
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:44,785
Programmer access.

314
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:49,624
- How do they work?
- A code is hidden in tumblers.

315
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:54,795
One position opens a lock and another
position opens one of these doors.

316
00:36:56,547 --> 00:36:59,383
Are you a programmer?

317
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:01,886
Then what are you?

318
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:07,558
I protect that which matters most.

319
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:30,456
Well, come on. I ain't gonna bite you.

320
00:37:30,873 --> 00:37:33,668
Come around here
and let me have a look at you.

321
00:37:36,879 --> 00:37:39,257
My goodness, look at you.

322
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:42,426
You turned out all right, didn't you?

323
00:37:42,593 --> 00:37:44,804
- How do you feel?
- I--

324
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:48,557
I know you're not sleeping.
We'll get to that.

325
00:37:48,724 --> 00:37:51,435
Why don't you come
and have a sit this time.

326
00:37:52,144 --> 00:37:56,274
- Maybe I'll stand.
- Well, suit yourself.

327
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:09,954
- I felt like sitting.
- I know.

328
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:13,040
So...

329
00:38:15,126 --> 00:38:17,545
...let's get the obvious stuff
out of the way.

330
00:38:17,837 --> 00:38:22,299
- You're not human, are you?
- It's tough to get more obvious than that.

331
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:28,306
If I had to guess, I'd say you're
a program from the machine world.

332
00:38:28,681 --> 00:38:32,893
- So is he.
- So far, so good.

333
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:36,230
But if that's true, that could mean
you're part of this system...

334
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:38,983
...another kind of control.

335
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:43,654
- Keep going.
- I suppose the most obvious question is...

336
00:38:43,821 --> 00:38:47,742
- ...how can I trust you?
- Bingo.

337
00:38:48,784 --> 00:38:52,038
It is a pickle, no doubt about it.
Bad news is...

338
00:38:52,204 --> 00:38:55,875
...there's no way you can really know
if I'm here to help you or not.

339
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:59,587
So it's really up to you. Just have
to make up your own damn mind...

340
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:04,550
...to either accept what
I'm going to tell you or reject it.

341
00:39:05,843 --> 00:39:08,012
Candy?

342
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:15,144
- Do you already know if I'll take it?
- Wouldn't be much of an oracle if I didn't.

343
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:18,522
But if you already know,
how can I make a choice?

344
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:22,735
Because you didn't come here to make
the choice. You've already made it.

345
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:27,531
You're here to try to understand
why you made it.

346
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:36,040
I thought you'd have figured that out
by now.

347
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:40,377
- Why are you here?
- Same reason.

348
00:39:40,628 --> 00:39:43,381
I love candy.

349
00:39:43,547 --> 00:39:46,384
But why help us?

350
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:50,054
We're all here to do
what we're all here to do.

351
00:39:50,596 --> 00:39:53,682
I'm interested in one thing, Neo:
the future.

352
00:39:53,849 --> 00:39:58,062
And believe me, I know, the only way
to get there is together.

353
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:03,818
- Are there other programs like you?
- Well, not like me, but...

354
00:40:03,984 --> 00:40:06,654
Look. See those birds?

355
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:10,282
At some point, a program was written
to govern them.

356
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:16,288
A program was written to watch over the
trees and the wind, the sunrise and sunset.

357
00:40:16,539 --> 00:40:19,417
There are programs running
all over the place.

358
00:40:19,583 --> 00:40:24,046
The ones doing their job, doing what
they were meant to do, are invisible.

359
00:40:24,213 --> 00:40:28,050
You'd never even know they were here.
But the other ones...

360
00:40:28,217 --> 00:40:32,304
Well, you hear about them all the time.

361
00:40:32,888 --> 00:40:35,766
- I've never heard of them.
- Of course you have.

362
00:40:35,933 --> 00:40:40,855
Every time you've heard someone
say they saw a ghost or an angel...

363
00:40:41,021 --> 00:40:45,609
...every story you've ever heard about
vampires, werewolves or aliens...

364
00:40:45,776 --> 00:40:48,112
...is the system assimilating
some program...

365
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:52,950
...that's doing something
they're not supposed to be doing.

366
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:56,120
Programs hacking programs.

367
00:40:56,287 --> 00:40:59,165
- Why?
- They have their reasons...

368
00:40:59,331 --> 00:41:03,294
...but usually a program chooses exile
when it faces deletion.

369
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:07,631
- And why would a program be deleted?
- Maybe it breaks down.

370
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:12,344
Maybe a better program is created
to replace it. Happens all the time.

371
00:41:12,511 --> 00:41:17,475
And when it does, a program
can either choose to hide here...

372
00:41:17,641 --> 00:41:20,311
...or return to the source.

373
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:25,274
- The machine mainframe.
- Yes.

374
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:27,943
Where you must go.

375
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:32,323
Where the path of the One ends.
You've seen it...

376
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:36,327
...in your dreams, haven't you?

377
00:41:36,493 --> 00:41:39,330
A door made of light?

378
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:45,127
What happens when you go through
the door?

379
00:41:47,254 --> 00:41:50,257
I see Trinity...

380
00:41:50,424 --> 00:41:53,594
...and something happens...

381
00:41:53,761 --> 00:41:55,679
...something bad.

382
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:59,850
She starts to fall,
and then I wake up.

383
00:42:00,893 --> 00:42:04,772
- Do you see her die?
- No.

384
00:42:05,564 --> 00:42:08,609
You have the sight now, Neo.

385
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:11,779
You are looking at the world
without time.

386
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:14,365
Then why can't I see
what happens to her?

387
00:42:14,531 --> 00:42:18,285
We can never see past the choices
we don't understand.

388
00:42:18,452 --> 00:42:21,622
Are you saying I have to choose
whether Trinity lives or dies?

389
00:42:21,872 --> 00:42:25,668
No, you've already made the choice.

390
00:42:25,834 --> 00:42:28,379
Now you have to understand it.

391
00:42:29,004 --> 00:42:30,381
No.

392
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:33,801
I can't do that. I won't.

393
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:36,887
- Well, you have to.
- Why?

394
00:42:37,471 --> 00:42:40,558
Because you're the One.

395
00:42:42,726 --> 00:42:45,729
What if I can't?

396
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:47,898
What happens if I fail?

397
00:42:48,482 --> 00:42:51,485
Then Zion will fall.

398
00:42:58,951 --> 00:43:03,831
Our time is up. Listen to me, Neo.
You can save Zion...

399
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:07,334
...if you reach the source, but to do that
you need the Keymaker.

400
00:43:07,501 --> 00:43:08,544
The Keymaker?

401
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:12,298
He disappeared. We didn't
know what happened to him until now.

402
00:43:12,464 --> 00:43:16,218
He's being held prisoner
by a very dangerous program...

403
00:43:16,385 --> 00:43:19,930
...one of the oldest of us.
He is called the Merovingian.

404
00:43:20,097 --> 00:43:22,975
- And he won't let him go willingly.
- What does he want?

405
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:27,980
What do all men with power want?
More power.

406
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:31,942
Be there at that exact time...

407
00:43:32,109 --> 00:43:34,778
...and you will have a chance.

408
00:43:35,571 --> 00:43:37,823
We must go.

409
00:43:37,990 --> 00:43:43,370
Seems like every time we meet
I got nothing but bad news.

410
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:46,707
I'm sorry about that. I surely am.

411
00:43:47,207 --> 00:43:49,752
But for what it's worth...

412
00:43:50,794 --> 00:43:54,465
...you've made a believer out of me.

413
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:57,885
Good luck, kiddo.

414
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:20,783
Mr. Anderson.

415
00:44:21,825 --> 00:44:23,827
Did you get my package?

416
00:44:23,994 --> 00:44:26,163
- Yeah.
- Well, good.

417
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:30,209
- Smith?
- He's not reading like an agent.

418
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:34,254
- Surprised to see me?
- No.

419
00:44:34,546 --> 00:44:37,007
- Then you're aware of it.
- Of what?

420
00:44:38,217 --> 00:44:40,219
Our connection.

421
00:44:40,386 --> 00:44:43,055
I don't fully understand how it happened.

422
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:46,600
Perhaps some part of you
imprinted onto me...

423
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:49,436
...something overwritten or copied.

424
00:44:49,603 --> 00:44:52,314
It is, at this point, irrelevant.
What matters is...

425
00:44:52,481 --> 00:44:55,567
...that whatever happened,
happened for a reason.

426
00:44:55,734 --> 00:44:57,403
And what reason is that?

427
00:44:57,861 --> 00:45:01,824
I killed you, Mr. Anderson.
I watched you die.

428
00:45:01,990 --> 00:45:05,244
With a certain satisfaction,
I might add.

429
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:08,914
And then something happened,
something that I knew was impossible...

430
00:45:09,081 --> 00:45:10,916
...but it happened anyway.

431
00:45:11,625 --> 00:45:14,795
You destroyed me, Mr. Anderson.

432
00:45:16,797 --> 00:45:21,385
Afterward, I knew the rules, I understood
what I was supposed to do...

433
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:24,555
...but I didn't.

434
00:45:24,972 --> 00:45:28,892
I couldn't. I was compelled to stay...

435
00:45:29,351 --> 00:45:32,896
...compelled to disobey.

436
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:37,234
And now, here I stand
because of you, Mr. Anderson.

437
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:41,363
Because of you, I'm no longer an agent
of this system.

438
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:44,741
Because of you, I've changed.
I'm unplugged.

439
00:45:44,908 --> 00:45:49,747
A new man, so to speak.
Like you, apparently free.

440
00:45:50,080 --> 00:45:51,457
Congratulations.

441
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:54,543
Thank you.

442
00:45:55,127 --> 00:45:59,756
But as you well know,
appearances can be deceiving...

443
00:45:59,923 --> 00:46:05,095
...which brings me back to the reason
why we're here.

444
00:46:05,262 --> 00:46:10,142
We're not here because we're free.
We're here because we are not free.

445
00:46:10,309 --> 00:46:14,229
There's no escaping reason,
no denying purpose.

446
00:46:14,396 --> 00:46:17,774
Because as we both know,
without purpose...

447
00:46:17,941 --> 00:46:22,779
- ...we would not exist.
- It is purpose that created us.

448
00:46:22,946 --> 00:46:25,949
- Purpose that connects us.
- Purpose that pulls us.

449
00:46:26,116 --> 00:46:27,951
- That guides us.
- That drives us.

450
00:46:28,118 --> 00:46:32,080
- It is purpose that defines.
- Purpose that binds us.

451
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:35,459
We are here because of you,
Mr. Anderson.

452
00:46:35,626 --> 00:46:40,005
We're here to take from you
what you tried to take from us:

453
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:44,051
Purpose.

454
00:46:47,137 --> 00:46:49,014
- What's happening to him?
- Don't know.

455
00:46:52,059 --> 00:46:55,646
Yes, that's it. It'll be over soon.

456
00:48:42,502 --> 00:48:44,963
- You.
- Yes, me.

457
00:48:49,134 --> 00:48:52,012
Me, me, me.

458
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:58,560
Me too.

459
00:51:06,313 --> 00:51:07,355
More.

460
00:52:09,626 --> 00:52:12,462
It is inevitable.

461
00:52:12,879 --> 00:52:14,297
Come on, get out of there.

462
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,843
Are you all right?

463
00:53:00,927 --> 00:53:02,846
- It was Smith.
- Yes.

464
00:53:03,722 --> 00:53:06,349
- Now there's more than one?
- A lot more.

465
00:53:06,516 --> 00:53:10,312
- How is that possible?
- I don't know.

466
00:53:10,478 --> 00:53:12,939
Somehow, he's found a way
to copy himself.

467
00:53:13,106 --> 00:53:17,319
- Is that what he was doing to you?
- I don't know what he was doing...

468
00:53:17,485 --> 00:53:20,238
- ...but I know what it felt like.
- What?

469
00:53:21,156 --> 00:53:24,868
It felt like I was back in that hallway.

470
00:53:25,035 --> 00:53:26,453
It felt like dying.

471
00:53:26,953 --> 00:53:29,831
The machines are tunneling to avoid
our defense system.

472
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:33,835
But I believe they will intersect
certain pipelines to control them.

473
00:53:34,002 --> 00:53:36,546
These points of intersection
are crucial...

474
00:53:36,713 --> 00:53:39,507
...because I believe they're
vulnerable to counterattack.

475
00:53:39,674 --> 00:53:43,720
Although it has been suggested that
this is the same kind of attack...

476
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:47,557
...we've defended for years,
I urge the Council to realize the truth.

477
00:53:47,724 --> 00:53:51,061
This is the single greatest threat
we have ever faced...

478
00:53:51,227 --> 00:53:55,065
...and if we do not act accordingly,
we will not survive.

479
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:59,236
Commander Lock, the Council is well
aware of the seriousness of this attack.

480
00:53:59,527 --> 00:54:04,074
You have our leave to prepare our defense
by any and all means necessary.

481
00:54:04,241 --> 00:54:06,910
- Thank you, Council.
- However...

482
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:10,497
...we ask if there's been word
from the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

483
00:54:10,747 --> 00:54:13,249
No, councillor. No word. Nothing.

484
00:54:14,876 --> 00:54:18,838
Then we request a ship be dispatched
to ascertain the fate of the One.

485
00:54:19,005 --> 00:54:22,759
I wish that were possible, councillor,
but I do not believe our defense...

486
00:54:22,926 --> 00:54:26,471
- ...can suffer the loss of another ship.
- It will, commander, if it must.

487
00:54:26,638 --> 00:54:28,974
It could take one ship days
to find the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

488
00:54:29,140 --> 00:54:32,185
- Then send two.
- This is insane.

489
00:54:32,352 --> 00:54:35,355
Careful, commander.

490
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:38,900
Forgive my frustration, councillors.

491
00:54:39,067 --> 00:54:42,946
But I wish I were able to comprehend
the Council's choice in this matter.

492
00:54:43,113 --> 00:54:46,283
Comprehension is not
a requisite of cooperation.

493
00:54:46,449 --> 00:54:48,910
If you are asking me
to order two of my captains--

494
00:54:49,077 --> 00:54:50,787
There's no need for such an order.

495
00:54:50,954 --> 00:54:54,499
The captains are present.
They can answer for themselves.

496
00:54:54,958 --> 00:55:00,213
The Council is calling for two volunteers
to aid the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

497
00:55:00,380 --> 00:55:04,551
Are there two among you
that would answer such a call?

498
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:09,639
Captain Soren of the <i>Vigilant</i>
will answer the Council's call.

499
00:55:09,806 --> 00:55:12,726
You understand the situation,
Captain Soren?

500
00:55:12,892 --> 00:55:15,353
- Yes, ma'am.
- Thank you, captain.

501
00:55:16,771 --> 00:55:18,189
Is there another?

502
00:55:18,982 --> 00:55:22,694
- Captain, I think we should volunteer.
- What? You have gone crazy.

503
00:55:22,861 --> 00:55:24,738
- Listen--
- Shut your hole, Bane...

504
00:55:24,904 --> 00:55:26,406
...before I put you in one.

505
00:55:27,574 --> 00:55:30,785
Captain Niobe of the <i>Logos</i>
will answer the councillor's call.

506
00:55:30,785 --> 00:55:32,120
- Thank you, Captain Niobe.

507
00:55:32,328 --> 00:55:37,417
Commander Lock, you have your orders.
This Council is hereby adjourned.

508
00:55:55,352 --> 00:55:56,770
What can you see, Neo?

509
00:55:56,936 --> 00:55:59,272
It's strange.
The code is somehow different.

510
00:55:59,439 --> 00:56:01,024
- Encrypted?
- Maybe.

511
00:56:01,191 --> 00:56:03,151
Is that good for us or bad for us?

512
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:06,988
Well, it looks like every floor
is wired with explosives.

513
00:56:07,614 --> 00:56:09,157
Bad for us.

514
00:56:09,574 --> 00:56:11,076
Here we go.

515
00:56:19,084 --> 00:56:22,003
Yes. We are here to speak
with the Merovingian.

516
00:56:22,462 --> 00:56:26,299
Well, of course.
He has been expecting you.

517
00:56:26,466 --> 00:56:27,509
Follow me.

518
00:56:48,196 --> 00:56:51,866
A-ha. Here he is at last.

519
00:56:52,075 --> 00:56:55,370
Neo, the One himself.

520
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:56,955
Right?

521
00:56:57,122 --> 00:56:59,457
And the legendary Morpheus.

522
00:57:00,291 --> 00:57:05,171
And Trinity, of course.
I have heard so much.

523
00:57:05,338 --> 00:57:08,800
You honor me. Please, sit. Join us.
This is my wife, Persephone.

524
00:57:09,717 --> 00:57:13,012
Something to eat? Drink?

525
00:57:13,304 --> 00:57:16,349
Of course, such things are contrivances,
like so much here.

526
00:57:16,516 --> 00:57:19,018
For the sake of appearances.

527
00:57:19,185 --> 00:57:22,647
- No, thank you.
- Yes, of course. Who has time?

528
00:57:22,814 --> 00:57:27,902
Who has time? But then, if we do not ever
take time, how can we ever have time?

529
00:57:31,865 --> 00:57:33,616
You know why we are here.

530
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:40,248
I am a trafficker of information.
I know everything I can.

531
00:57:40,665 --> 00:57:46,504
The question is,
do you know why you are here?

532
00:57:46,796 --> 00:57:49,257
We are looking for the Keymaker.

533
00:57:49,924 --> 00:57:54,429
Oh, yes, it is true.
The Keymaker, of course.

534
00:57:54,596 --> 00:57:57,557
But this is not a reason,
this is not a why.

535
00:57:57,724 --> 00:58:01,477
The Keymaker himself, his very nature,
is a means, it is not an end.

536
00:58:01,644 --> 00:58:07,400
And so to look for him is to be
looking for a means to do...

537
00:58:07,567 --> 00:58:10,737
- ...what?
- You know the answer to that question.

538
00:58:10,904 --> 00:58:13,031
But do you?

539
00:58:13,239 --> 00:58:15,575
You think you do, but you do not.

540
00:58:15,742 --> 00:58:18,953
You are here
because you were sent here.

541
00:58:19,120 --> 00:58:22,248
You were told to come here,
and then you obeyed.

542
00:58:23,416 --> 00:58:25,752
It is, of course, the way of all things.

543
00:58:25,919 --> 00:58:28,588
You see, there is only one constant...

544
00:58:28,755 --> 00:58:32,926
...one universal. It is the only real truth.

545
00:58:33,092 --> 00:58:34,761
Causality.

546
00:58:34,928 --> 00:58:37,222
Action, reaction.

547
00:58:37,388 --> 00:58:41,601
- Cause and effect.
- Everything begins with choice.

548
00:58:41,768 --> 00:58:43,519
No. Wrong.

549
00:58:43,686 --> 00:58:48,274
Choice is an illusion created
between those with power...

550
00:58:48,441 --> 00:58:50,526
...and those without.

551
00:58:50,985 --> 00:58:56,449
Our only hope, our only peace,
is to understand it, to understand the why.

552
00:58:56,616 --> 00:59:00,036
"Why" is what separates us from them...

553
00:59:00,203 --> 00:59:02,497
...you from me.

554
00:59:02,664 --> 00:59:06,417
"Why" is the only real source of power.
Without it, you are powerless.

555
00:59:06,584 --> 00:59:09,879
And this is how you come to me,
without why, without power.

556
00:59:10,046 --> 00:59:12,840
Another link in the chain.

557
00:59:13,049 --> 00:59:14,342
But fear not.

558
00:59:14,509 --> 00:59:18,388
Since I have seen how good you are
at following orders...

559
00:59:18,555 --> 00:59:21,182
...I will tell you what to do next.

560
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:26,521
Run back and give the fortuneteller
this message:

561
00:59:26,729 --> 00:59:30,984
Her time is almost up.

562
00:59:32,026 --> 00:59:35,571
Now I have some real business to do,
so I will say <i>adieu</i> and goodbye.

563
00:59:35,738 --> 00:59:38,241
- This isn't over.
- Oh, yes, it is.

564
00:59:38,408 --> 00:59:44,789
The Keymaker is mine, and I see no reason
why I should give him up.

565
00:59:44,956 --> 00:59:49,002
- No reason at all.
- Where are you going?

566
00:59:49,168 --> 00:59:53,881
Please, <i>ma chérie,</i> I have told you.
We are all victims of causality.

567
00:59:54,048 --> 00:59:57,385
I drank too much wine,
I must take a piss.

568
00:59:57,885 --> 01:00:01,014
Cause and effect. <i>Au revoir.</i>

569
01:00:09,272 --> 01:00:10,773
Well, that didn't go so well.

570
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:13,318
Are you certain the Oracle
didn't say anything else?

571
01:00:13,484 --> 01:00:15,611
- Yes.
- Maybe we did something wrong.

572
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:17,613
Or didn't do something.

573
01:00:17,780 --> 01:00:21,034
No, what happened couldn't have
happened any other way.

574
01:00:21,200 --> 01:00:23,953
- How do you know?
- We are still alive.

575
01:00:27,248 --> 01:00:30,501
If you want the Keymaker, follow me.

576
01:01:05,536 --> 01:01:07,288
Not again.

577
01:01:10,708 --> 01:01:13,336
It's all right, boys. They're with me.

578
01:01:14,003 --> 01:01:16,381
These fellas work for my husband.

579
01:01:16,547 --> 01:01:20,385
They do his dirty work.
They're very good, very loyal.

580
01:01:20,551 --> 01:01:22,095
Aren't you, boys?

581
01:01:22,261 --> 01:01:23,304
Yes, mistress.

582
01:01:23,471 --> 01:01:26,182
They come from a much older version
of the Matrix.

583
01:01:26,349 --> 01:01:30,520
But like so many back then, they caused
more problems than they solved.

584
01:01:31,270 --> 01:01:36,275
My husband saved them because
they're notoriously difficult to terminate.

585
01:01:36,442 --> 01:01:40,488
How many people keep silver bullets
in their gun?

586
01:01:45,201 --> 01:01:48,413
You can either run and tell my husband
what I have done...

587
01:01:48,579 --> 01:01:51,165
...or you can stay there and die.

588
01:01:52,083 --> 01:01:54,043
He's in the ladies' room!

589
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:02,051
Hurry.

590
01:02:27,618 --> 01:02:30,788
- My name is Neo.
- Yes. I'm the Keymaker.

591
01:02:30,955 --> 01:02:32,874
I've been waiting for you.

592
01:02:38,796 --> 01:02:43,384
Oh! My God! My God, Persephone,
how could you do this? You betray me.

593
01:02:47,722 --> 01:02:50,558
- Cause and effect, my love.
- Cause?

594
01:02:50,725 --> 01:02:53,728
There is no cause for this. What cause?

595
01:02:53,895 --> 01:02:58,191
What cause? How about the lipstick
you're still wearing?

596
01:02:58,357 --> 01:03:01,068
Lipstick? Lipstick.

597
01:03:01,235 --> 01:03:05,072
What craziness are you talking about,
woman? There is no lipstick!

598
01:03:06,783 --> 01:03:09,452
She wasn't kissing your face, my love.

599
01:03:10,578 --> 01:03:15,041
Aye-yi-yi-yi.
Woman, this is nothing.

600
01:03:15,208 --> 01:03:20,755
- It is a game. It is only a game.
- So is this.

601
01:03:20,922 --> 01:03:22,924
Have fun.

602
01:03:29,430 --> 01:03:31,098
All right.

603
01:03:31,265 --> 01:03:33,017
All right.

604
01:03:33,267 --> 01:03:36,062
Let us find out where this goes.

605
01:03:36,229 --> 01:03:39,106
You two, get the Keymaker.

606
01:03:45,613 --> 01:03:47,615
That's a nice trick.

607
01:03:47,782 --> 01:03:49,075
I cannot go back.

608
01:03:49,617 --> 01:03:51,619
I'll handle them.

609
01:03:52,119 --> 01:03:58,251
Handle us? You'll handle us? You know,
your predecessors had much more respect.

610
01:04:11,639 --> 01:04:13,683
Okay, you have some skill.

611
01:04:15,893 --> 01:04:17,854
Kill him.

612
01:05:18,039 --> 01:05:20,082
You see? He's just a man.

613
01:07:34,884 --> 01:07:37,636
Goddamn it, woman,
you will be the end of me.

614
01:07:39,764 --> 01:07:43,768
Mark my words, boy,
and mark them well.

615
01:07:43,934 --> 01:07:49,148
I have survived your predecessors,
and I will survive you.

616
01:08:09,210 --> 01:08:12,588
- Where are you going?
- Another way. Always another way.

617
01:08:16,717 --> 01:08:18,594
Close it, quick!

618
01:08:23,390 --> 01:08:25,935
Could we move along?

619
01:08:29,480 --> 01:08:31,065
Run!

620
01:08:46,080 --> 01:08:49,333
Step away from the door.

621
01:08:54,421 --> 01:08:55,714
We owe you for that.

622
01:08:57,967 --> 01:08:59,134
Just like new.

623
01:08:59,426 --> 01:09:00,886
Drop your weapon.

624
01:09:06,267 --> 01:09:08,102
- Stay with him.
- What about Neo?

625
01:09:08,269 --> 01:09:09,812
He can handle himself.

626
01:09:12,898 --> 01:09:13,983
Get in back.

627
01:09:51,645 --> 01:09:52,813
Shit.

628
01:09:53,314 --> 01:09:54,815
- Operator.
<i>- Link, where am I?</i>

629
01:09:55,357 --> 01:09:58,569
You won't believe this,
but you're way up in the mountains.

630
01:09:58,861 --> 01:10:01,155
- Really?
- <i>It'll take me a while to get an exit.</i>

631
01:10:01,655 --> 01:10:02,698
- Shit!
- <i>What?</i>

632
01:10:02,907 --> 01:10:05,576
The twins are after Morpheus and Trinity.
They don't have a way out.

633
01:10:05,743 --> 01:10:09,121
- Where are they?
- <i>Middle of the city, 500 miles due south.</i>

634
01:10:25,888 --> 01:10:27,473
<i>- Operator.</i>
- Get us out of here.

635
01:10:27,640 --> 01:10:30,392
- <i>Won't be easy.</i>
- I know. We're inside the core network.

636
01:10:30,559 --> 01:10:33,187
<i>The only exit I got
near you is the Winslow overpass.</i>

637
01:10:33,354 --> 01:10:35,439
- Off the freeway.
- <i>Yes, sir.</i>

638
01:10:35,606 --> 01:10:39,360
- Fine, we'll make it.
- <i>I should-- Oh, shit! Look out behind you!</i>

639
01:10:44,365 --> 01:10:45,950
- Incoming fire.
- Down!

640
01:10:54,208 --> 01:10:55,376
Hold on!

641
01:11:12,393 --> 01:11:14,895
Oh, no. This is getting real ugly
real fast.

642
01:11:15,062 --> 01:11:16,772
Are you watching this, Link?

643
01:11:16,939 --> 01:11:20,567
Yes, sir. There's an all points on you.
Eight units headed your way.

644
01:11:21,610 --> 01:11:23,570
Any suggestions?

645
01:11:25,447 --> 01:11:27,449
- Turn right.
- Right, now.

646
01:11:34,915 --> 01:11:37,751
Straight here.
You'll hit a connecting tunnel to the 101.

647
01:11:37,918 --> 01:11:39,295
- Good man.

648
01:11:39,461 --> 01:11:41,630
You always told me
to stay off the freeway.

649
01:11:41,797 --> 01:11:44,425
- Yes, that's true.
- You said it was suicide.

650
01:11:44,633 --> 01:11:46,552
Then let us hope...

651
01:11:46,719 --> 01:11:48,095
...that I was wrong.

652
01:11:59,982 --> 01:12:01,066
- Operator.
- Link, it's Niobe.

653
01:12:01,233 --> 01:12:02,860
We've been sent to bring you in.

654
01:12:03,027 --> 01:12:06,113
- I need to talk to Morpheus.
- Believe me, Niobe, he needs you.

655
01:12:06,280 --> 01:12:08,282
- <i>Where is he?</i>
- Just follow the sirens.

656
01:12:15,831 --> 01:12:17,750
Repeat, they're approaching the--

657
01:12:20,919 --> 01:12:25,132
- We have them now.
- The exile is the primary target.

658
01:13:28,278 --> 01:13:29,738
<i>Shots fired.</i>

659
01:13:32,366 --> 01:13:34,243
Move!

660
01:15:24,228 --> 01:15:27,439
- We are getting aggravated.
- Yes, we are.

661
01:16:13,485 --> 01:16:15,487
Trinity.

662
01:16:15,904 --> 01:16:17,030
Get him out of here.

663
01:16:20,659 --> 01:16:22,744
Come on!

664
01:16:39,761 --> 01:16:41,263
Crush him.

665
01:17:11,752 --> 01:17:12,794
Morpheus.

666
01:17:12,961 --> 01:17:14,463
He's okay. Keep moving.

667
01:17:15,464 --> 01:17:17,257
Let's go.

668
01:17:23,013 --> 01:17:25,182
I need a download
to hot-wire a motorcycle.

669
01:17:25,349 --> 01:17:27,684
No problem.
One crash course on motorcycle--

670
01:17:27,851 --> 01:17:29,269
Wait.

671
01:17:30,646 --> 01:17:32,105
Cancel that.

672
01:17:32,272 --> 01:17:34,483
You are handy.

673
01:17:34,650 --> 01:17:36,568
Jump on.

674
01:20:03,840 --> 01:20:04,883
She means nothing.

675
01:20:05,050 --> 01:20:08,178
- Find the exile.
- We have them.

676
01:20:08,512 --> 01:20:10,639
<i>One-Adam-12, please respond.</i>

677
01:20:17,103 --> 01:20:18,813
Get down.

678
01:22:29,819 --> 01:22:31,446
Gotcha.

679
01:22:32,197 --> 01:22:33,281
She's good.

680
01:22:37,661 --> 01:22:39,955
You are no longer necessary.

681
01:22:46,628 --> 01:22:50,340
We do only what we're meant to do.

682
01:22:51,967 --> 01:22:55,553
Then you are meant for one more thing:
deletion.

683
01:22:56,513 --> 01:22:58,390
Go kick his ass.

684
01:23:48,440 --> 01:23:51,192
Neo, if you're out there,
I could use some help.

685
01:23:51,943 --> 01:23:53,403
What is that?

686
01:24:23,266 --> 01:24:26,144
Yes! Yes!

687
01:24:32,734 --> 01:24:37,864
We have confirmation from the <i>Icarus.</i> First
two ships are in position for counterattack.

688
01:24:38,114 --> 01:24:39,157
Good.

689
01:24:40,158 --> 01:24:41,201
Any change?

690
01:24:41,367 --> 01:24:44,120
They hit some iron ore here.
Slowed them down a little.

691
01:24:44,287 --> 01:24:47,415
- How much?
- An hour, maybe.

692
01:24:47,582 --> 01:24:50,126
That would give them
a little over nine hours.

693
01:24:50,960 --> 01:24:52,587
Yes, sir.

694
01:25:25,203 --> 01:25:27,455
<i>There is a building.</i>

695
01:25:27,622 --> 01:25:33,294
Inside this building, there is a level
where no elevator can go...

696
01:25:33,461 --> 01:25:35,380
...and no stair can reach.

697
01:25:36,047 --> 01:25:42,137
<i>This level is filled with doors.
These doors lead to many places.</i>

698
01:25:42,303 --> 01:25:44,639
Hidden places.

699
01:25:44,973 --> 01:25:48,601
But one door is special.

700
01:25:48,768 --> 01:25:50,979
One door leads to the source.

701
01:25:59,320 --> 01:26:03,741
This building is protected
by a very secure system.

702
01:26:03,908 --> 01:26:06,744
- Every alarm triggers the bomb.
- Bomb? Did he say bomb?

703
01:26:06,870 --> 01:26:09,539
But like all systems,
it has a weakness.

704
01:26:09,706 --> 01:26:12,709
The system is based on the rules
of a building.

705
01:26:12,876 --> 01:26:16,254
- One system built on another.
- Electricity.

706
01:26:16,796 --> 01:26:21,551
- If one fails, so must the other.
- No electricity, no alarms.

707
01:26:21,718 --> 01:26:24,554
You'd have to take out a city block
to kill the power.

708
01:26:24,721 --> 01:26:28,433
- Not one, 27.
- Twenty-seven blocks?

709
01:26:29,267 --> 01:26:31,728
<i>There is a power station.</i>

710
01:26:31,895 --> 01:26:34,147
<i>It must be destroyed.</i>

711
01:26:34,314 --> 01:26:38,651
- There must be some kind of fail-safe.
- Yes, there is an emergency system.

712
01:26:40,278 --> 01:26:44,073
<i>The core network of the grid
must be accessed.</i>

713
01:26:44,240 --> 01:26:47,076
<i>The emergency system
must be deactivated.</i>

714
01:26:47,243 --> 01:26:48,661
<i>What do you need us for?</i>

715
01:26:48,828 --> 01:26:50,079
Neo could take them out
easier than we could.

716
01:26:51,164 --> 01:26:52,916
- There's no time.
- Why?

717
01:26:53,082 --> 01:26:56,210
Once the door is unprotected,
the connection will be severed.

718
01:26:56,377 --> 01:26:58,671
But another connection
must first be made.

719
01:26:59,505 --> 01:27:03,343
<i>- How long will that take?</i>
<i>- Exactly 314 seconds.</i>

720
01:27:03,509 --> 01:27:05,094
<i>Just over five minutes.</i>

721
01:27:05,261 --> 01:27:07,513
<i>That is the length
and breadth of the window.</i>

722
01:27:07,680 --> 01:27:09,974
Only the One can open the door...

723
01:27:10,183 --> 01:27:13,102
...and only during that window
can the door be opened.

724
01:27:14,354 --> 01:27:15,939
How do you know all this?

725
01:27:16,105 --> 01:27:21,277
I know because I must know.
It is my purpose.

726
01:27:21,444 --> 01:27:26,950
It's the reason I'm here,
the same reason we're all here.

727
01:27:37,710 --> 01:27:40,505
Neo, I know something's wrong.

728
01:27:41,172 --> 01:27:43,216
You don't have to tell me.

729
01:27:43,383 --> 01:27:47,136
I just want you to know that I'm here.

730
01:27:50,682 --> 01:27:52,141
All must be done as one.

731
01:27:54,560 --> 01:27:56,229
If one fails...

732
01:27:57,021 --> 01:27:58,731
<i>...all fail.</i>

733
01:27:59,232 --> 01:28:02,902
At midnight, there is a shift change
in the security of both buildings.

734
01:28:04,279 --> 01:28:07,532
<i>At midnight, we will strike.</i>

735
01:28:08,157 --> 01:28:09,242
Hey!

736
01:28:09,409 --> 01:28:13,371
- You count sheep at home.
- Why? I get paid to count them here.

737
01:28:23,548 --> 01:28:25,758
Okay, they're inside.

738
01:28:25,925 --> 01:28:28,428
- How much time?
- Twelve minutes.

739
01:28:31,139 --> 01:28:32,223
Oh, shit.

740
01:28:35,601 --> 01:28:41,065
All of our lives, we have fought this war.
Tonight, I believe we can end it.

741
01:28:42,567 --> 01:28:44,736
<i>Tonight is not an accident.</i>

742
01:28:46,070 --> 01:28:48,072
<i>There are no accidents.</i>

743
01:28:49,449 --> 01:28:54,495
We have not come here by chance.
I do not believe in chance.

744
01:28:54,662 --> 01:29:00,251
When I see three objectives,
three captains, three ships...

745
01:29:00,418 --> 01:29:03,921
...I do not see coincidence.
I see providence.

746
01:29:04,255 --> 01:29:06,591
<i>I see purpose.</i>

747
01:29:09,302 --> 01:29:15,641
I believe it is our fate to be here.
It is our destiny.

748
01:29:15,808 --> 01:29:20,813
I believe this night holds
for each and every one of us...

749
01:29:20,980 --> 01:29:24,317
...the very meaning of our lives.

750
01:29:24,484 --> 01:29:28,654
I want to ask you to do something,
but I don't know how.

751
01:29:29,238 --> 01:29:31,157
I promise you, if I can, I will.

752
01:29:32,492 --> 01:29:35,828
What if I asked you to stay out of this...

753
01:29:36,788 --> 01:29:38,790
...no matter what...

754
01:29:38,956 --> 01:29:41,292
...to stay out of the Matrix?

755
01:29:42,376 --> 01:29:44,170
Why?

756
01:29:52,387 --> 01:29:53,471
Please.

757
01:29:55,556 --> 01:29:56,891
All right.

758
01:30:00,228 --> 01:30:02,730
What is it, Niobe?

759
01:30:02,897 --> 01:30:07,026
I can't help it, Morpheus. I can't
help thinking, what if you're wrong?

760
01:30:07,193 --> 01:30:10,488
What if all this, the prophecy,
everything, is bullshit?

761
01:30:10,655 --> 01:30:14,659
Then tomorrow we may all be dead.

762
01:30:15,076 --> 01:30:17,703
But how would that be different
from any other day?

763
01:30:27,171 --> 01:30:33,678
This is a war, and we are soldiers.

764
01:30:33,928 --> 01:30:36,848
<i>Death can come for us at any time...</i>

765
01:30:37,390 --> 01:30:39,183
<i>...in anyplace.</i>

766
01:30:39,350 --> 01:30:41,269
Incoming. Incoming!

767
01:30:43,229 --> 01:30:44,856
Incoming!

768
01:30:50,778 --> 01:30:53,239
Now consider the alternative.

769
01:30:53,406 --> 01:30:57,994
What if I am right?
What if the prophecy is true?

770
01:30:58,161 --> 01:31:02,582
What if tomorrow the war could be over?

771
01:31:03,541 --> 01:31:06,544
Isn't that worth fighting for?

772
01:31:07,670 --> 01:31:10,298
Isn't that worth dying for?

773
01:31:11,215 --> 01:31:13,843
- Time?
- Three minutes.

774
01:31:14,010 --> 01:31:15,136
Almost there.

775
01:31:35,198 --> 01:31:36,574
It is done.

776
01:31:36,741 --> 01:31:38,034
Find the others.

777
01:31:39,160 --> 01:31:41,412
I got Niobe there.
They're out of the station.

778
01:31:41,579 --> 01:31:44,248
- What about Soren?
- There.

779
01:31:44,415 --> 01:31:46,250
They're still inside, but...

780
01:31:47,126 --> 01:31:48,169
They're not moving.

781
01:32:12,318 --> 01:32:14,237
That's it, let's go.

782
01:32:16,364 --> 01:32:18,199
Call Neo now.

783
01:32:22,161 --> 01:32:24,080
- I lost them. They're inside the portal.
- What about the grid?

784
01:32:29,126 --> 01:32:32,630
Everything is operational.
The emergency system is rerouting power.

785
01:32:38,302 --> 01:32:40,471
Jesus.

786
01:32:40,638 --> 01:32:44,684
Soon as they open that door,
it's all over.

787
01:32:44,850 --> 01:32:46,811
The hell it is.

788
01:32:47,562 --> 01:32:48,896
What are you--? Trinity!

789
01:32:50,189 --> 01:32:53,150
I will not wait and do nothing.
I will not watch them die.

790
01:32:53,317 --> 01:32:55,486
We're talking less than five minutes.

791
01:32:55,653 --> 01:32:58,155
In five minutes,
I'll tear that building down.

792
01:32:58,322 --> 01:33:01,867
- How much further?
- Here, just here.

793
01:33:03,160 --> 01:33:07,164
I'm sorry, this is a dead end.

794
01:33:08,332 --> 01:33:10,835
It's gotta be the ugliest hack
I have ever done.

795
01:33:14,046 --> 01:33:17,174
That's as close as I can get you.
You better grow wings.

796
01:33:35,776 --> 01:33:36,819
- Operator.
<i>- I'm in.</i>

797
01:33:36,986 --> 01:33:39,155
Keep moving. Sixty-fifth floor.

798
01:33:39,739 --> 01:33:43,909
You look surprised to see me again,
Mr. Anderson.

799
01:33:44,076 --> 01:33:49,457
Well, that's the difference between us.
I have been expecting you.

800
01:33:49,624 --> 01:33:52,543
- What do you want, Smith?
- You haven't figured that out?

801
01:33:52,710 --> 01:33:58,215
Still using all the muscles
except the one that matters.

802
01:33:58,382 --> 01:34:01,052
I want exactly what you want.

803
01:34:01,218 --> 01:34:03,304
I want everything.

804
01:34:03,763 --> 01:34:06,265
Would that include a bullet
from this gun?

805
01:34:06,432 --> 01:34:08,225
Go ahead, shoot.

806
01:34:08,392 --> 01:34:13,689
The best thing about being me,
there's so many me's.

807
01:34:25,076 --> 01:34:28,704
Christ! What the hell happened in here?

808
01:34:29,580 --> 01:34:31,624
Hold it right there, little lady.

809
01:34:40,966 --> 01:34:42,760
If you can't beat us...

810
01:34:42,927 --> 01:34:44,762
Join us.

811
01:34:46,931 --> 01:34:48,015
Morpheus!

812
01:35:01,612 --> 01:35:04,740
Still no sight of them.
They only got two minutes left.

813
01:35:18,504 --> 01:35:19,547
One minute.

814
01:35:28,764 --> 01:35:29,807
Come on.

815
01:35:30,975 --> 01:35:32,893
Come on.

816
01:35:33,477 --> 01:35:35,354
Please.

817
01:35:45,281 --> 01:35:46,824
Kill them.

818
01:35:54,707 --> 01:35:55,750
They're in.

819
01:35:55,916 --> 01:35:57,877
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

820
01:36:13,434 --> 01:36:15,561
It was meant to be.

821
01:36:15,728 --> 01:36:21,108
Morpheus, that door will take you home.

822
01:36:29,867 --> 01:36:34,205
You will know which door.
Hurry, Neo.

823
01:36:39,710 --> 01:36:42,880
Trinity, I got some serious activity
headed your way.

824
01:37:35,182 --> 01:37:36,559
Hello, Neo.

825
01:37:37,101 --> 01:37:40,896
- Who are you?
- I am the Architect.

826
01:37:41,063 --> 01:37:44,692
I created the Matrix.
I've been waiting for you.

827
01:37:44,942 --> 01:37:49,113
You have many questions. Though the
process has altered your consciousness...

828
01:37:49,280 --> 01:37:51,282
...you remain irrevocably human.

829
01:37:51,448 --> 01:37:55,035
Ergo, some of my answers you will
understand and some you will not.

830
01:37:55,452 --> 01:37:59,498
Concordantly, while your first question
may be the most pertinent...

831
01:37:59,665 --> 01:38:03,377
...you may or may not realize
it is also the most irrelevant.

832
01:38:04,253 --> 01:38:05,879
Why am I here?

833
01:38:06,046 --> 01:38:09,967
Your life is the sum of a remainder
of an unbalanced equation...

834
01:38:10,134 --> 01:38:12,469
...inherent to the programming
of the Matrix.

835
01:38:12,636 --> 01:38:16,724
You are the eventuality of an anomaly,
which despite my sincerest efforts...

836
01:38:16,891 --> 01:38:19,727
...I've been unable to eliminate
from what is otherwise...

837
01:38:19,893 --> 01:38:24,356
...a harmony of mathematical precision.

838
01:38:24,690 --> 01:38:27,026
While it remains a burden
assiduously avoided...

839
01:38:27,192 --> 01:38:31,655
...it is not unexpected and thus
not beyond a measure of control...

840
01:38:31,822 --> 01:38:35,784
...which has led you, inexorably...

841
01:38:36,744 --> 01:38:37,995
...here.

842
01:38:38,162 --> 01:38:42,249
- You haven't answered my question.
- Quite right.

843
01:38:42,416 --> 01:38:46,211
Interesting.
That was quicker than the others.

844
01:38:46,378 --> 01:38:49,006
<i>Others? How many?
What others?</i>

845
01:38:49,173 --> 01:38:51,675
The Matrix is older than you know.

846
01:38:51,842 --> 01:38:55,846
I count from the emergence of one integral
anomaly to the emergence of the next.

847
01:38:56,013 --> 01:38:58,265
In which case, this is the sixth version.

848
01:38:58,432 --> 01:39:00,893
<i>Five before me?
He's lying. Bullshit.</i>

849
01:39:01,060 --> 01:39:04,605
<i>There are only two possible explanations.
There were five before me.</i>

850
01:39:04,772 --> 01:39:06,065
<i>Either no one told me...</i>

851
01:39:07,316 --> 01:39:11,320
- ...or no one knows.
- Precisely.

852
01:39:11,487 --> 01:39:14,782
As you are undoubtedly gathering,
the anomaly is systemic...

853
01:39:14,949 --> 01:39:18,369
...creating fluctuations in even
the most simplistic equations.

854
01:39:18,535 --> 01:39:21,789
<i>You can't control me!
I'm gonna smash you to bits!</i>

855
01:39:21,955 --> 01:39:23,749
<i>I'm gonna fucking kill you!</i>

856
01:39:23,916 --> 01:39:27,086
<i>You can't make me do anything.
You old, white prick!</i>

857
01:39:29,380 --> 01:39:30,881
Choice.

858
01:39:31,048 --> 01:39:32,883
The problem is choice.

859
01:39:55,114 --> 01:39:58,742
The first Matrix I designed
was naturally perfect, a work of art.

860
01:39:58,909 --> 01:40:00,744
Flawless, sublime.

861
01:40:00,911 --> 01:40:04,415
A triumph equaled only
by its monumental failure.

862
01:40:05,082 --> 01:40:07,501
The inevitability of its doom
is apparent now...

863
01:40:07,668 --> 01:40:11,004
...as a consequence of the imperfection
inherent in every human.

864
01:40:11,171 --> 01:40:14,133
Thus, I redesigned it
based on your history...

865
01:40:14,299 --> 01:40:18,303
...to more accurately reflect
the varying grotesqueries of your nature.

866
01:40:19,013 --> 01:40:22,766
However, I was again frustrated
by failure.

867
01:40:24,226 --> 01:40:26,854
I have come to understand
that the answer eluded me...

868
01:40:27,021 --> 01:40:29,064
...because it required a lesser mind.

869
01:40:29,231 --> 01:40:35,195
Or perhaps, a mind less bound
by the parameters of perfection.

870
01:40:35,612 --> 01:40:40,034
Thus, the answer was stumbled upon
by another, an intuitive program...

871
01:40:40,200 --> 01:40:44,079
...initially created to investigate
certain aspects of the human psyche.

872
01:40:45,164 --> 01:40:51,128
If I am the father of the Matrix,
she would undoubtedly be its mother.

873
01:40:51,754 --> 01:40:54,048
- The Oracle.
- Please.

874
01:40:54,757 --> 01:40:58,761
As I was saying, she stumbled upon a
solution whereby 99 percent of subjects...

875
01:40:58,927 --> 01:41:01,805
...accepted the program, as long as they
were given a choice...

876
01:41:01,972 --> 01:41:06,101
...even if they were only aware
of the choice at a near unconscious level.

877
01:41:06,268 --> 01:41:09,688
While this answer functioned,
it was fundamentally flawed...

878
01:41:09,855 --> 01:41:13,859
...thus creating the otherwise
contradictory systemic anomaly...

879
01:41:14,026 --> 01:41:16,737
...that, if left unchecked,
might threaten the system.

880
01:41:17,112 --> 01:41:21,241
Ergo, those that refused the program,
while a minority, if unchecked...

881
01:41:21,408 --> 01:41:25,496
...would constitute
an escalating probability of disaster.

882
01:41:25,662 --> 01:41:27,456
This is about Zion.

883
01:41:27,915 --> 01:41:31,585
You are here because Zion
is about to be destroyed.

884
01:41:31,752 --> 01:41:36,173
Its every living inhabitant terminated,
its entire existence eradicated.

885
01:41:36,465 --> 01:41:37,508
Bullshit.

886
01:41:37,674 --> 01:41:40,844
Denial is the most predictable
of all human responses.

887
01:41:41,053 --> 01:41:47,518
But rest assured, this will be
the sixth time we have destroyed it...

888
01:41:47,684 --> 01:41:51,688
...and we have become
exceedingly efficient at it.

889
01:42:04,409 --> 01:42:05,702
The function of the One...

890
01:42:05,869 --> 01:42:10,541
...is now to return to the source, allowing
a dissemination of the code you carry...

891
01:42:10,707 --> 01:42:12,417
...reinserting the prime program.

892
01:42:13,001 --> 01:42:17,005
After which you will be required to select
from the Matrix 23 individuals...

893
01:42:17,172 --> 01:42:20,425
...sixteen female, seven male,
to rebuild Zion.

894
01:42:20,592 --> 01:42:25,138
Failure to comply with this process
will result in a cataclysmic system crash...

895
01:42:25,305 --> 01:42:27,641
...killing everyone connected
to the Matrix...

896
01:42:27,808 --> 01:42:30,394
...which, coupled with the
extermination of Zion...

897
01:42:30,561 --> 01:42:34,773
...will result in the extinction
of the entire human race.

898
01:42:35,107 --> 01:42:39,194
You won't let it happen. You can't.
You need human beings to survive.

899
01:42:39,987 --> 01:42:43,615
There are levels of survival
we are prepared to accept.

900
01:42:43,782 --> 01:42:46,577
The relevant issue is
whether or not you are ready...

901
01:42:46,743 --> 01:42:50,330
...to accept the responsibility for the death
of every human being in this world.

902
01:42:56,795 --> 01:42:59,339
It is interesting reading your reactions.

903
01:43:00,382 --> 01:43:04,219
Your five predecessors were, by design,
based on a similar predication...

904
01:43:04,386 --> 01:43:08,849
...a contingent affirmation that was meant
to create a profound attachment...

905
01:43:09,016 --> 01:43:12,603
...to the rest of your species,
facilitating the function of the One.

906
01:43:12,769 --> 01:43:15,105
While the others experience this
in a general way...

907
01:43:15,272 --> 01:43:18,233
...your experience is far more specific...

908
01:43:18,567 --> 01:43:21,445
...vis-à-vis love.

909
01:43:22,446 --> 01:43:24,072
Trinity!

910
01:43:26,366 --> 01:43:30,704
Apropos, she entered the Matrix
to save your life at the cost of her own.

911
01:43:31,079 --> 01:43:32,122
No.

912
01:43:32,831 --> 01:43:36,960
Which brings us at last to the moment
of truth, wherein the fundamental flaw...

913
01:43:37,127 --> 01:43:40,214
...is ultimately expressed
and the anomaly revealed...

914
01:43:40,380 --> 01:43:44,384
...as both beginning and end.

915
01:43:44,551 --> 01:43:46,219
There are two doors.

916
01:43:46,386 --> 01:43:49,598
The door to your right leads to the source
and the salvation of Zion.

917
01:43:50,182 --> 01:43:56,480
The door to your left leads back to the
Matrix, to her and the end of your species.

918
01:43:56,647 --> 01:44:01,026
As you adequately put,
the problem is choice.

919
01:44:01,193 --> 01:44:04,696
But we already know what
you are going to do, don't we?

920
01:44:04,863 --> 01:44:08,951
Already I can see the chain reaction,
the chemical precursors that signal...

921
01:44:09,117 --> 01:44:14,373
...the onset of an emotion designed
specifically to overwhelm logic and reason.

922
01:44:14,539 --> 01:44:19,169
An emotion that is already blinding you
from the simple and obvious truth:

923
01:44:19,336 --> 01:44:25,842
She is going to die and there is nothing
you can do to stop it.

924
01:44:30,847 --> 01:44:34,977
Hope. It is the quintessential
human delusion, simultaneously...

925
01:44:35,143 --> 01:44:38,855
...the source of your greatest strength
and your greatest weakness.

926
01:44:39,022 --> 01:44:43,360
If I were you, I would hope
that we don't meet again.

927
01:44:43,527 --> 01:44:44,945
We won't.

928
01:44:52,369 --> 01:44:54,579
We got a serious situation, sir.

929
01:44:55,038 --> 01:44:56,123
Oh, no.

930
01:45:55,766 --> 01:45:59,311
- What was that?
- It's moving faster than anything I've seen.

931
01:47:03,667 --> 01:47:05,502
Neo, I had to.

932
01:47:05,669 --> 01:47:07,420
I know.

933
01:47:12,467 --> 01:47:15,011
The bullet is still inside.

934
01:47:25,772 --> 01:47:27,691
Trinity...

935
01:47:28,900 --> 01:47:30,610
...don't you quit on me now.

936
01:47:39,786 --> 01:47:42,372
I'm sorry.

937
01:47:48,879 --> 01:47:51,173
Trinity.

938
01:48:01,141 --> 01:48:03,101
Trinity...

939
01:48:03,268 --> 01:48:05,061
...I know you can hear me.

940
01:48:05,854 --> 01:48:08,398
I'm not letting go.

941
01:48:08,565 --> 01:48:10,192
I can't.

942
01:48:11,401 --> 01:48:13,612
I love you too damn much.

943
01:48:42,307 --> 01:48:43,600
I can't take this.

944
01:48:47,354 --> 01:48:50,440
I guess this makes us even.

945
01:49:03,119 --> 01:49:05,080
I don't understand it.

946
01:49:05,247 --> 01:49:08,250
Everything was done
as it was supposed to be done.

947
01:49:08,416 --> 01:49:11,461
Once the One reaches the source,
the war should be over.

948
01:49:11,628 --> 01:49:14,464
- In 24 hours, it will be.
- What?

949
01:49:14,631 --> 01:49:18,969
If we don't do something in 24 hours,
Zion will be destroyed.

950
01:49:19,386 --> 01:49:21,012
- What?
- How do you know that?

951
01:49:21,471 --> 01:49:23,515
- I was told it would happen.
- By whom?

952
01:49:24,516 --> 01:49:27,352
It doesn't matter. I believed him.

953
01:49:27,519 --> 01:49:31,356
- That's impossible. The prophecy tells us--
- It was a lie, Morpheus.

954
01:49:33,108 --> 01:49:35,652
The prophecy was a lie.

955
01:49:36,861 --> 01:49:39,864
The One was never meant
to end anything.

956
01:49:39,114 --> 01:49:43,076
It was all another system of control.

957
01:49:43,243 --> 01:49:46,329
I don't believe that.

958
01:49:46,663 --> 01:49:48,081
But you said it yourself.

959
01:49:49,165 --> 01:49:53,169
How can the prophecy be true
if the war isn't over?

960
01:49:59,342 --> 01:50:01,803
I'm sorry.

961
01:50:01,970 --> 01:50:05,348
I know it isn't easy to hear, but...

962
01:50:05,515 --> 01:50:08,685
...I swear to you it's the truth.

963
01:50:11,896 --> 01:50:14,607
- What are we gonna do?
- I don't know.

964
01:50:16,818 --> 01:50:18,028
Oh, no!

965
01:50:27,370 --> 01:50:30,707
- What are they doing?
- They're just out of EMP range.

966
01:50:31,207 --> 01:50:32,459
It's a bomb.

967
01:50:33,626 --> 01:50:35,837
We have to get out of here. Now.

968
01:51:12,540 --> 01:51:14,417
I have dreamed a dream...

969
01:51:17,462 --> 01:51:20,840
...but now that dream
has gone from me.

970
01:51:31,893 --> 01:51:34,145
Here they come.

971
01:51:34,396 --> 01:51:36,106
Let's go, Morpheus.

972
01:51:37,524 --> 01:51:40,568
- We won't make it.
- We have to try.

973
01:51:48,284 --> 01:51:51,287
- Come on!
- Something's different.

974
01:51:51,454 --> 01:51:53,456
What?

975
01:51:54,124 --> 01:51:55,625
I can feel them.

976
01:52:18,565 --> 01:52:20,150
Neo!

977
01:52:26,322 --> 01:52:29,909
- What happened?
- I don't know.

978
01:52:35,165 --> 01:52:37,083
It's the <i>Hammer.</i>

979
01:52:48,762 --> 01:52:51,473
He's in some kind of coma...

980
01:52:51,639 --> 01:52:53,892
...but his vitals are stable.

981
01:52:55,101 --> 01:52:57,020
What about you?

982
01:52:57,187 --> 01:52:59,314
I'm fine.

983
01:52:59,481 --> 01:53:01,858
You could use some rest.

984
01:53:02,025 --> 01:53:03,860
No, I'm gonna stay with him.

985
01:53:10,950 --> 01:53:13,578
Lock was right.
He guessed that the machines...

986
01:53:13,745 --> 01:53:16,623
...would cut <i>off</i> the mainlines
in and out of Zion.

987
01:53:16,790 --> 01:53:19,542
He thought a counterattack
might surprise them.

988
01:53:19,793 --> 01:53:23,213
It sounded good.
I figured we had a shot...

989
01:53:23,546 --> 01:53:26,090
...until someone screwed it up.

990
01:53:26,257 --> 01:53:28,885
An EMP was triggered before
we got in position.

991
01:53:29,052 --> 01:53:30,929
Five ships were instantly downed.

992
01:53:31,095 --> 01:53:32,889
When the machines broke through...

993
01:53:33,056 --> 01:53:36,267
...it wasn't a battle, it was a slaughter.

994
01:53:36,434 --> 01:53:39,270
Was it an accident?
Some sort of malfunction?

995
01:53:39,437 --> 01:53:41,898
- No one knows.
- Someone does.

996
01:53:42,065 --> 01:53:43,816
Who?

997
01:53:43,983 --> 01:53:47,695
Once the machines were done with us,
they started digging again.

998
01:53:47,862 --> 01:53:50,156
We made a quick pass
to look for survivors.

999
01:53:50,365 --> 01:53:51,449
You found one?

1000
01:53:53,201 --> 01:53:54,911
Only one.

1001
02:03:48,003 --> 02:03:51,298
<i>Everything that has a beginning...</i>

1002
02:03:51,465 --> 02:03:53,175
<i>...has an end.</i>

1003
02:03:55,594 --> 02:03:58,472
<i>I see the end coming.</i>

1004
02:03:58,639 --> 02:04:02,434
<i>I see the darkness spreading.
I see death.</i>

1005
02:04:04,562 --> 02:04:07,565
Mr. Anderson, welcome back.

1006
02:04:07,731 --> 02:04:09,733
We missed you.

1007
02:04:09,900 --> 02:04:11,735
It ends tonight.

1008
02:04:18,951 --> 02:04:22,079
<i>You are all that stands in his way.</i>

1009
02:04:23,664 --> 02:04:28,210
<i>If you cannot stop him tonight,
then I fear that tomorrow may never come.</i>

